{
  "$comment": "CHECKS (#EXP-1613; src/checks.ts, ecode-core checks.rs). A check row = one CI job's result at a PR's head: {name, status (contract checkStatus), conclusion (checkConclusion, null until completed)}. `rollup`: none (no rows) · failure (any completed row whose conclusion is in checkConclusion.failing; wins over pending) · pending (any not completed) · success; the same rule as domain-contract pr-checks `aggregateChecksState`, and apps/web/src/lib/ecode/ecode-spec.test.ts replays these rows on both. `gate` over the REQUIRED names (none named = every row gates; a required name without a row is `missing`): blocked (a gated row failed) · no_checks (nothing required, no rows) · waiting (a gated row not completed, or a required name missing) · ready; `failing`, `pending` and `missing` list names in row order (missing in required order). `checkName`: a job's check name is its name, plus its matrix values as ` (a, b)`. Our CI writes these rows into `commit_checks` + `pull_request_checks`, so the Merge pill, the wake-ups and the merge train read our CI and GitHub Actions alike.",
